## why the current predicate is a tautology (HOME-independence of the candidate primitives)
  bun : homedir()=/tmp/fakehome  userInfo().homedir=/tmp/fakehome
  node: homedir()=/tmp/fakehome  userInfo().homedir=/root
  -> under node userInfo() is passwd-derived (/root); under bun it FOLLOWS HOME, so the recommended
     one-line fix works in production (dsh is node: #!/usr/bin/env node) but not under bun/tests.

## the four shapes x two runtimes (guard invoked exactly as a QA boot does)
  node sandbox HOME     : REFUSED code=real-home-refused status=403
  node HOME unset       : REFUSED code=real-home-refused status=403
  node HOME=/root (real): REFUSED code=real-home-refused status=403
  node sandbox+override : ALLOWED
  bun  sandbox HOME     : REFUSED code=real-home-refused status=403
  bun  HOME unset       : REFUSED code=real-home-refused status=403
  bun  HOME=/root (real): REFUSED code=real-home-refused status=403
  bun  sandbox+override : ALLOWED

## the production runtime
  dsh: /root/.nvm/versions/node/v24.16.0/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/lib/bin.js
  shebang: #!/usr/bin/env node

## verdict
  ROW 1 (the sanctioned recipe: HOME=<sandbox> + DSH_HOME set) is REFUSED 403 in BOTH runtimes = the bug.
  The guard therefore refuses the sandbox and cannot distinguish it from the real home, because
  homedir() IS $HOME: the comparison 'resolve(home) !== resolve(realHome)' is false in every boot.
